# Citation metadata for this repository (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
# Drafted by task T4 from README.md and the papers' title pages. Every field marked TODO
# was not found in the repository and is left for a human. See LICENSES.md for the
# licence that applies to each directory.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository, cite it as below. Until the tag v0.1.0-pre exists,
  pin the commit you used and say so (decision D10). No DOI is minted yet.
type: software
title: "theory_mono-repo: the addressability programme"
abstract: >-
  The canonical record of one theory, written as four documents that share a single
  inequality, D^{-1} d_S(u,v) - K <= d_M(addr u, addr v), and of the reference frame
  it licenses. Everything here is either a theorem (machine-checked in Lean 4 where the
  kernel reaches, cited where it does not), a registered measurement (registration dated
  before its data, verdict scored by the registered rule, readings kept separate), or a
  named open question. The repository holds Paper I (The Addressability Limit), Paper II
  (Evolution as Active Geometry: Descent Under the Addressability Limit), the note
  (The Structured Addressability Limit), the BRF2026 datum specification sheet, the Lean 4
  modules added to the kernel, and the registered record (PREREG00 to 25).
